4... Bc5 { That's the Classical Variation. We need to fight for our only developed piece. } (4... Qf6 { Other move orders can lead to the same final position. } 5. Be3 (5. c3 Bc5 6. Be3) 5... Bc5 6. c3) 5. Be3 { The Knight could capture Black’s Knight with a tempo on the Queen and win the Bishop afterward. } { [%csl Gc6][%cal Ge3c5,Gc6d8] } 5... Qf6 (5... Nf6 6. Nxc6 bxc6 (6... dxc6 7. Qxd8+ Kxd8 8. Bxc5) 7. Bxc5) 6. c3 Nge7 { Black moves the Knight to prepare for castling. } { [%cal Ge8h8] } 7. Bc4 { We’re moving the Bishop to prepare for castling as well. } { [%cal Ge1h1] } 7... O-O 8. O-O *


