[FEN "r1bqkbnr/pppp1ppp/2n5/8/3NP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R b KQkq - 0 4"]
[SetUp "1"]
[UTCDate "2025.10.09"]
[UTCTime "02:23:14"]
[Orientation "white"]

4... Nf6 { That's the Schmidt Variation, it's the main line. We want to exchange Knights and then push the central Pawn. } { [%cal Gd4c6,Ge4e5] } 5. Nxc6 bxc6 (5... dxc6 { Capturing with the Queen’s Pawn would simply trade Queens and lose castling rights, with no benefits. } 6. Qxd8+ Kxd8 7. f3 { [%cal Gf3e4] }) 6. e5 { That's the Mieses Variation. We expand in the center and attack the Knight. } { [%cal Ge5f6] } 6... Qe7 { The Queen defends the Knight by pinning the Pawn. } { [%cal Ge7e1] } (6... Nd5 { We can again attack the Knight with tempo. } 7. c4 { [%cal Gd5b6,Gd5e7] }) 7. Qe2 { The Queen shelters the King and unpins the Pawn. } { [%cal Ge5f6] } 7... Nd5 8. c4 { Black can either pin the Pawn with the Bishop, threatening the Queen, or simply move the Knight to safety. } { [%csl Gc4][%cal Gc8a6,Ga6e2,Gd5b6] } *


